          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: A witness reports to GEIPAN numerous observations of PAN made from their home in CAP-D'AIL (06). Investigation of this case proved impossible for the following reasons (see investigation report):\n\n- The initial questionnaire submitted to GEIPAN concerns several observations that are either poorly documented or not documented at all, which do not appear to have an obvious connection with the two attached photographs. It is also noted that the witness mentioned the date of January 20, 2022, without it being associated with a specific observation.\n\n- In response to the investigator's request for clarification, the witness sends an email that does not refer to their initial observations but discusses a different observation than the one mentioned in the questionnaire. This email is accompanied by several photographs related to other observations than the one initially reported.\n\n- An examination of both documents (questionnaire and email) reveals the existence of at least 6 distinct observations, either photographic or testimonial (but never both simultaneously), which were all found to be completely unusable due to a more or less significant lack of essential data that would have allowed their study.\n\nGEIPAN classifies the case as \"C\": multiple observations for which the significant lack of data does not allow for analysis to be considered.",
          "translation_text_sha256": "877b2559712e94625a2a774377dc8019b88b3a9581f88191be1d0130fd4cf783"
        }
